{
  "name": "Video to Audio - LTX-2",
  "author": "Invoke",
  "description": "Generate a soundtrack for an existing clip with LTX-2.5. The clip's frames are held fixed and only the audio is generated; the output is your footage with the new stereo soundtrack.",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "contact": "",
  "tags": "ltx, ltx2, video, audio, video to audio, v2a, soundtrack",
  "notes": "The clip decides the length and frame rate: there are no controls for them. A clip whose frame rate the gallery does not know cannot be used here. Describe the sound you want in the prompt; the model also infers it from what is on screen.\n\nEach InvokeAI install assigns its own internal model IDs, so the model fields ship blank -- pick these in the form after loading (all from the LTX-2.5 starter bundle):\n\n- Model: LTX-2.5 Dev Transformer (int8) or LTX-2.5 Distilled Transformer (int8). The Denoise node's 'auto' schedule follows the checkpoint: Dev runs the guided 30-step recipe, Distilled a fixed 8 steps with no guidance (its Steps and guidance values are ignored, and the log says so).\n- Components: LTX-2.5 Components (VAEs, vocoder, text connectors, latent upscaler).\n- Text Encoder: LTX-2.5 Text Encoder (Gemma-4 12B, int8). Required: no LTX-2 model carries one.\n\nThe negative prompt is pre-filled with the release's own default list and is used only on Dev with a CFG or Audio CFG above 1. On Distilled, turning off 'Encode Negative' on the Prompt node skips its encode.\n\nTarget Resolution: use 512p, 704p or 768p. A held picture cannot run a two-stage refine pass, and this template takes the base canvas, so 1024p/1536p encode at half their named size.",
  "exposedFields": [
    {
      "nodeId": "source_clip",
      "fieldName": "video"
    },
    {
      "nodeId": "positive_prompt",
      "fieldName": "value"
    },
